<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 41,100 in March.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 41,100 in March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in March and average earnings in February. (Previous estimates in brackets, minus denotes fall, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>    UNEMPLOYMENT		   MARCH	FEB	(PREL FEB)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		-41,100    -66,400   (-68,200)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)		     6.1*	 6.2	    (6.2)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change  -82,500     n/a	(-80,000)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate     6.2	  6.5	    (6.5)</p>
<p>NOTE - Mkts forecast 45,000 March unemployment fall  </p>
<p>    Unemployment level (million) 1.707	1.748	(1.746)</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj     1.745	1.828	(1.827)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m adj   -58,700    -60,600   (-61,200)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m	 -60,600    -60,100   (-60,400)</p>
<p>   AVERAGE EARNINGS		     FEB	JAN  (PREL JAN)</p>
<p>   underlying yearly chng (pct)     5.0	4.75	(5.0)</p>
<p>   index (base 1990)		    136.0    136.3   (136.3)</p>
<p>   actual yearly chng (pct)	   4.1	4.9	 (4.9)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>   Production-- underlying	    4.75     4.75	(5.0)</p>
<p>		 -- actual		  4.1	4.3	 (4.3)</p>
<p>    Manufacturing -- underlying     4.75     4.75     (4.75)</p>
<p>			-- actual	   4.4	4.2	 (4.2)</p>
<p>    Services	-- underlying     5.0	4.75	(5.0)</p>
<p>			-- actual	   4.2	5.2	 (5.2)</p>
<p>NOTE: consensus forecast 4.75 pct for overall underlying average earnings.</p>
<p>    UNIT WAGE COSTS		     FEB	JAN  (PREL JAN)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago	  2.4	2.5	 (2.7)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		   115.4    115.0   (115.2)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago	  2.6	3.1	 (3.1)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		   115.4    115.3   (115.3)</p>
<p>    PRODUCTIVITY			  FEB	JAN  (PREL JAN)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago	  1.8	1.6	 (1.5)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		   122.8    122.3   (122.1)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago	  1.9	1.5	 (1.4)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		   122.4    122.0   (121.9)</p>
<p>OVERALL EMPLOYMENT (THOUSANDS, S/ADJ)</p>
<p>    WORKFORCE IN EMPLOYMENT	   Q4     Q3	  Q4 1995</p>
<p>    LEVEL				   26,147 26,100     25,925</p>
<p>    CHANGE				  47     216	  148</p>
<p>    EMPLOYEES IN EMPLOYMENT  LEVEL  22,363 22,308     22,142</p>
<p>				    CHANGE  54     115	  145</p>
<p>    JOB CENTRE VACANCIES		MARCH     FEB   (PREL FEB)</p>
<p>    change				 +3,500    +8,500   (+7,800)</p>
<p>    level				  275,100   271,600 (270,900)</p>
<p>    Avg 3m change			+2,900    +1,000     (+700)</p>
<p>* The ONS said the unemployment level is at it lowest since September 1990 with the rate lower than at any time since October 1990.</p>
<p>Annualised average earnings growth are their highest since November 1992.</p>
<p>The inflow of vacancies at job centres, 249,500 in March, was the highest on record.  </p>
<p>The ONS said the figures continue to be distorted by the Jobseekers Allowance. The recorded unemployment falls over the last six months suggest the rate of fall is now higher than it was in mid-1996 -- i.e. higher than 15-20,000 per month.</p>
